Unpopular opinion:
you don't owe your family a relationship.

Everyone says they're still your family.
So let's look at what family did.

A mother of six was told losing one child wouldn't be a big deal, since she had five more.
Grandparents skipped visiting their dying grandson because they didn't want to miss casino night.
A woman was asked when she'd get a boyfriend, two months after her fiancé died of cancer.

And when you finally say it hurt,
you're told you're too sensitive.
You're told it was years ago and you should let it go.

Being related to someone is not a free pass.
Family isn't who shares your blood.
It's who shows up.

Would you cut them off? Be honest.
